<%# locals: (name:, agent: nil, portrait: nil, role: nil) %>
<%# The shell's head (agent_chats/_shell): the page's agent, its portrait a big circle centered on top, its name and role under it. Alex on /build, the CTO once the app exists. The portrait keeps ONE view-transition name on every agent page, so Build my app morphs Alex's portrait into the CTO's. `agent` is an Agent row (components/agent_avatar); `portrait` is ready markup that wins over it; with neither, the name's initial on a plain circle. `role` is ready markup or text. An explicit local, never a bare yield: a partial rendered without a block yields the LAYOUT's body. The agent-shell-* classes are the shell's compaction hooks (app/assets/tailwind/agent_shell.css): the portrait shrinks and the caption joins it on one line as the conversation grows. %>
<div class="agent-shell-header flex flex-col items-center gap-2 text-center min-w-0" data-test="agent-chat-header" data-agent-name="<%= name %>">
  <div class="agent-shell-portrait rounded-full shadow-md" style="view-transition-name: agent-portrait;" data-test="agent-portrait">
    <% if portrait %>
      <%= portrait %>
    <% elsif agent %>
      <%= render "components/agent_avatar", agent: agent, size: "xl" %>
    <% else %>
      <span class="w-24 h-24 text-3xl rounded-full flex items-center justify-center bg-inset border border-subtle text-heading font-bold shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"><%= name.to_s.first.upcase %></span>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <p class="agent-shell-caption text-sm text-secondary break-words" style="view-transition-name: agent-caption;" data-test="agent-caption">
    <span class="font-semibold text-heading"><%= name %></span><% if role.present? %> · <%= role %><% end %>
  </p>
</div>
